The string "PAYPALISHIRING" is written in a zigzag pattern on a given number of rows like this: (you may want to display this pattern in a fixed font for better legibility)

P   A   H   N
A P L S I I G
Y   I   R
And then read line by line: "PAHNAPLSIIGYIR"

Write the code that will take a string and make this conversion given a number of rows:

string convert(string s, int numRows);
 

Example 1:

Input: s = "PAYPALISHIRING", numRows = 3
Output: "PAHNAPLSIIGYIR"
Example 2:

Input: s = "PAYPALISHIRING", numRows = 4
Output: "PINALSIGYAHRPI"
Explanation:
P     I    N
A   L S  I G
Y A   H R
P     I
Example 3:

Input: s = "A", numRows = 1
Output: "A"
#write code here:-
char* convert(char* s, int numRows) {
    if (numRows == 1 || numRows >= strlen(s)) {
        return s;
    }

    int len = strlen(s);
    char* result = (char*)malloc((len + 1) * sizeof(char));
    int idx = 0;
    int cycleLen = 2 * numRows - 2;
    for (int i = 0; i < numRows; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j + i < len; j += cycleLen) {
            // 1. Add the main vertical character down the column
            result[idx++] = s[j + i];
            
            // 2. Add the inner diagonal character (not applicable for first and last rows)
            int diagonalIdx = j + cycleLen - i;
            if (i != 0 && i != numRows - 1 && diagonalIdx < len) {
                result[idx++] = s[diagonalIdx];
            }
        }
    }
    result[idx] = '\0';
    return result;
}
